   "widgets_values": [
    "## upscale-seedvr2.json\n\nSeedVR2 upscale / restore, with a before/after slider\n\nU1 - SeedVR2 (Apache 2.0) replaces the non-commercial 4x-UltraSharp. RESOLUTION IS THE SHORT EDGE, not a multiplier: resolution=2048 on a 1024 input gives 2048. batch_size must follow 4n+1 (use 1 for a single still). color_correction='lab' is the recommended highest-fidelity mode. 24 GB -> 7B fp16 with no memory tricks (offload_device=none on the loaders); drop to 3B fp16 or 7B fp8 + blocks_to_swap/offloading if it OOMs. Measured vs 4x-UltraSharp at 2x: more reconstructed detail (grad-var 137.0 vs 97.7) but more drift from the source (2.70 vs 1.29) and slower (39 s vs 6 s) - it regenerates rather than enlarges.\n**Slider:** `ImageCompare` shows the source against the result; the `SaveImage` is the deliverable.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S10** in `HOWTO.md`  \u00b7  Why it is this way: **U1/E13f** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*"
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## upscale-seedvr2.json\n\nSeedVR2 upscale / restore, with a before/after slider\n\nU1 - SeedVR2 (Apache 2.0) replaces the non-commercial 4x-UltraSharp. RESOLUTION IS THE SHORT EDGE, not a multiplier: resolution=2048 on a 1024 input gives 2048. batch_size must follow 4n+1 (use 1 for a single still). color_correction='lab' is the recommended highest-fidelity mode. 24 GB -> 7B fp16 with no memory tricks (offload_device=none on the loaders); drop to 3B fp16 or 7B fp8 + blocks_to_swap/offloading if it OOMs. Measured vs 4x-UltraSharp at 2x: more reconstructed detail (grad-var 137.0 vs 97.7) but more drift from the source (2.70 vs 1.29) and slower (39 s vs 6 s) - it regenerates rather than enlarges.\n**Slider:** `ImageCompare` shows the source against the result; the `SaveImage` is the deliverable.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S10** in `HOWTO.md`  \u00b7  Why it is this way: **U1/E13f** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*"
   },
